11. Missing Values

This is very important in Data Science.

| Method      | Use                         | Example        |
| ----------- | --------------------------- | -------------- |
| `isna()`    | Find missing values         | `df.isna()`    |
| `isnull()`  | Find missing values         | `df.isnull()`  |
| `notna()`   | Find non-missing values     | `df.notna()`   |
| `notnull()` | Find non-missing values     | `df.notnull()` |
| `dropna()`  | Remove missing rows/columns | `df.dropna()`  |
| `fillna()`  | Fill missing values         | `df.fillna(0)` |
| `ffill()`   | Forward fill                | `df.ffill()`   |
| `bfill()`   | Backward fill               | `df.bfill()`   |

===

Example
df["Age"] = df["Age"].fillna(df["Age"].mean())

Meaning:

Replace missing Age values with the average Age.

